## Interpretation

The app-level cached handler p99 in the stage sample is 133.032 ms, while the Locust-observed p99 after the best fix is 7900 ms. That gap points to runtime queueing, process instability, local load-generator pressure, or another layer outside the sampled query handler.

The blocked prompt path is still a measurable hot path, but its sampled P99 is 433.396 ms and cannot explain the full multi-second aggregated C4 tail by itself. Attempts to add workers and tune audit lock retry timing regressed results; the audit lock timing change was reverted.
